ws Homer well: The entire Phaeacian episode is gone; Matt Damonâ€™s Odysseus never meets his father. Where the Homeric epic splits and gives its hero 12 books on Ithaca, the movie is about two-thirds journey and flashback with under an hour once Odysseus returns home. The middle of Christopher Nolanâ€™s The Odyssey (2026) delivers visceral discomfort. When the witch Circe (Samantha Morton) serves her transformative feast to Odysseusâ€™s companions on the island of Aeaea, the camera tracks their voracious hunger, following their shift from greedily slurping, increasingly frantic men into squealing pigs. Circe physically wrests them out of one shape into another, later commenting that their appetites made them what they truly are. Read More SPONSORED Mitchell Johnson: New Paintings from California, New England and Europe Work by the Bay Area artist is on view in Menlo Park, California, through August 29. Learn more News Cuban dissident performance artist Luis Manuel Otero AlcÃ¡ntara arrived in Miami on Saturday, July 18, after over a week of ambiguity surrounding his whereabouts following his scheduled release from a five-year sentence for â€œcontempt, defamation, and public disorder.â€ Just weeks before a historic collection of 20th-century Mexican art is slated to leave the country for an exhibition in Europe, a group of advocates is suing Mexicoâ€™s principal cultural entity over allegations regarding the legal basis for exporting the nationâ€™s artistic heritage. Following a legal battle between the city of Philadelphia and the Trump administration, federal officials replaced exhibits describing the history of slavery in the United States at a Pennsylvania historical park. Just a few months after the reopening of the New Museumâ€™s expanded building, a water leak shut down the Manhattan institution for a full weekend. From Our Critics The Sunflower Effect of Kyung-Me The artistâ€™s current series marks a shift in her practice, evoking the life span of a sunflower â€” from blooming to dying, from sharply defined forms to rivulets of dissolution. | John Yau Read More From the Archive Why Did Roman Baths Disappear? New research contests the myth that it was Christianityâ€™s opposition to public nudity that led to the decline in large-scale bathing in the late Roman Empire. | Sarah Bond Read Moreƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;PDT0zY5FAI8Q8ueIo1fDxHHNRAcReq7iXAJyBx4Thtwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;Unm6Htkmbd2okJ0yraFjabhrOU4-9xOTXOw0mItTECsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;8aM3VhlxlkSu1IKrtZfPzKBTITDa577rGW_3TucRrlgƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;g-iCJO2sju3nXvgJE295FaHEevsaaCiSUWIKvTt9RBoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;yBxKOVt5PBn_LISO8l5xN8sSpJPd8SVqEhljvp1pYOwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;o_Zw1-GIO9o3m0WpMOxBW3oegMKrcpTgBLia5C0xKr8ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;kVAv2rMTyFjQOJzSP4yt1ID3VMlh25PA9PgRlX2IICcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lAx7vX-JHNUgmuoLexF2YLtACunvKfhywU8yXCSo1Hwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;XMI9c5wrjDnuYZ-iQP6rNv26dfvj8aTQY7ffGBiPjxMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx(urn:rmn:predicate:source-reports-su